{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-eta-mu-release-2-0-1-1792441718933", :event/time "2026-10-19T20:28:38.933Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "eta-mu-release-2-0-1", :text "open-hax/eta-mu#360 opened; CodeRabbit round 1 finding (schema introduced-by, P2) fixed in e4e12a09 and settled. Codex quota-unavailable. Required checks verify, Rheos tests and lint, rheos-github-sync fail only because ETA_MU_APP_ID/ETA_MU_APP_PRIVATE_KEY are unset on open-hax/eta-mu (secrets live on riatzukiza forks). Decision needed: set org secrets or run the PR on the fork.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1792441718931-0.lyo5v4xqhhf9ero1o1h", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "e3be20b5-bfaf-4ba9-9520-3bd4bac0ed3e"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-eta-mu-release-2-0-1-1792442575208", :event/time "2026-10-19T20:42:55.208Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "eta-mu-release-2-0-1", :text "Correction: the earlier note that ETA_MU_APP_ID/ETA_MU_APP_PRIVATE_KEY are unset on open-hax/eta-mu was unverified (org secrets are not readable with the current token). #360's head is the riatzukiza fork, and GitHub withholds secrets from fork-originated pull_request runs even when org secrets exist, which fits the 'unavailable' failures. Decision: run the review on riatzukiza/eta-mu as a same-repo PR.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1792442575205-0.hseipw42ljw4t8qh6vc", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "822acd4f-e737-46dd-ac39-8b192710cebf"}
