{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-ae0dc0b3-31f6-4f2c-872b-81f387296add-1792929735509", :event/time "2026-10-25T12:02:15.509Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "ae0dc0b3-31f6-4f2c-872b-81f387296add", :dependency [], :parent nil, :card-type "epic", :type "task-created", :write-id "1792929735508-0.fw8xg0u1vrkftd29xnq", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Qualify native review intent for the shared-login release", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/qualify-native-review-intent-for-the-shared-login-release-87296add.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Qualify native review intent for the shared-login release\n\n## Context\n\nPlanning source: https://github.com/riatzukiza/.agents/pull/47 . Prerequisite merged classifier: https://github.com/riatzukiza/.agents/pull/45 . This is an initial-state planning card; independent review and lawful Rheos transitions are still required. No model label grants approval, a completed round, settlement, CI or deployment credit.\n\n## Outcome\n\nObserve complete raw native review intent, qualify an independent body-assessment/publication purpose, then consume fresh revocable evidence in canonical disposition without changing approval authority.\n\n## Scope\n\nCanonical owner: riatzukiza/.agents. Protected assessment, invocation, App publication and readback owner: open-hax/eta-mu. Fleet consumers remain their own application and Services repositories.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo installed gate activation, approval recognition, provider/account grant, paid fallback, host cutover, board-policy clone or fabricated native evidence.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Three child slices have reviewed standalone acceptance criteria and explicit dependencies.\n- [ ] Actual requests remain obligations beside acknowledgements, including unmarked, contradictory and P0/P1 content.\n- [ ] Canonical and protected ETA changes are reviewed separately; native full-input, permission, identity, history, runtime and one-shot readback proof precede adoption.\n- [ ] All reviewer, round, CI, unresolved-thread and immutable fleet release gates remain in force.\n\n## Verification\n\nRetain authentic and explicitly derived adversarial source, model/prompt/schema/runtime identity and actual native evidence. Source planning and local fixtures do not establish runtime qualification. The protected source/profile and append-only history must be reviewed before operational adoption.\n\n## Risks\n\nSemantic omissions, prompt injection, confused identities, stale edits/history, mixed requests and acknowledgements, uncertain publication, and accidental conversion of triage into approval must remain visible and fail closed."}, :causal/root "e2b128e9-f1d6-4df7-b4bb-44380f3051f9"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-d1acd458-3e9b-4641-afb7-50e34d51703b-1792929736010", :event/time "2026-10-25T12:02:16.010Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "d1acd458-3e9b-4641-afb7-50e34d51703b", :dependency [], :parent "ae0dc0b3-31f6-4f2c-872b-81f387296add", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1792929736008-0.l8ceo6pjhlst4xxbdev", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Collect fresh native review source for advisory classification", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/collect-fresh-native-review-source-for-advisory-classification-4d51703b.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Collect fresh native review source for advisory classification\n\n## Context\n\nPlanning source: https://github.com/riatzukiza/.agents/pull/47 . Prerequisite merged classifier: https://github.com/riatzukiza/.agents/pull/45 . This is an initial-state planning card; independent review and lawful Rheos transitions are still required. No model label grants approval, a completed round, settlement, CI or deployment credit.\n\n## Outcome\n\nReuse the canonical native collector and bounded classifier; preserve complete raw source, exact native identity, permission/edit/history/head custody and advisory provenance.\n\n## Scope\n\nCanonical owner: riatzukiza/.agents. Protected assessment, invocation, App publication and readback owner: open-hax/eta-mu. Fleet consumers remain their own application and Services repositories.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo installed gate activation, approval recognition, provider/account grant, paid fallback, host cutover, board-policy clone or fabricated native evidence.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Incomplete pages, REST/GQL mismatch, changed head/body/edit/permissions/history and unavailable history refuse.\n- [ ] Model JSON accounts for every source unit; lost units, forged hashes, ambiguous quotes, low confidence, transport errors and truncation stay unresolved.\n- [ ] Derived source addresses preserve exact offsets/body hash and never masquerade as native IDs; ambiguous obligation correspondence stays blocked.\n- [ ] Tests exercise actual collector and transport boundaries; a valid result still grants only advisory authority.\n\n## Verification\n\nRetain authentic and explicitly derived adversarial source, model/prompt/schema/runtime identity and actual native evidence. Source planning and local fixtures do not establish runtime qualification. The protected source/profile and append-only history must be reviewed before operational adoption.\n\n## Risks\n\nSemantic omissions, prompt injection, confused identities, stale edits/history, mixed requests and acknowledgements, uncertain publication, and accidental conversion of triage into approval must remain visible and fail closed."}, :causal/root "891602b5-bc54-4a51-852e-f3c7a0ce8a33"}
