{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-18ef840f-23cb-4dd5-bc19-a2a5aeb279c3-1793718671885", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:11:11.885Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "18ef840f-23cb-4dd5-bc19-a2a5aeb279c3", :dependency ["0db50b53-6c7a-489a-bff9-048d57ce4cbb" "e616187d-ba13-42b1-addd-aa4d6244a5be"], :parent "e842e6d9-dd41-4ca2-b229-dc2466198864", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1793718671883-0.tc597wqt1co3d4vjf", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Oikos: Qualify 12B backends and governed proxx comparison after admission", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/oikos-qualify-12b-backends-and-governed-proxx-comparison-after-admission-aeb279c3.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Oikos: Qualify 12B backends and governed proxx comparison after admission\n\n## Context\n\nPlanning only for private open-hax/oikos at /home/err/spaces/foresight/oikos. Desktop is a local-first shared workbench. Initial incoming proposal; planning review is not complete. Creation authorizes no implementation, live configuration, deployment, inference, upload or spending. This focused slice belongs to Oikos: empirical local Gemma and OCR qualification.\n\n## Outcome\n\nQualify 12B backends and governed proxx comparison after admission.\n\n## Scope\n\nPrepare and execute only separately admitted comparisons against E4B and existing NPU PP-OCR baseline.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo claim 4B is inherently too dumb, port8082 deployment readiness, implicit cloud admission, model download or heavy live benchmark this turn.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Pin official 12B identity, quantization and context; CPU/GPU/NPU OpenVINO support is measured or explicitly unsupported, never inferred from OCR.\n- [ ] Fresh resource admission precedes downloads/launch; deny OOM-disruptive tests. Verify proxx gemma4:31b route/free claim from dated evidence; use only GovOne-admitted sanitized fixtures.\n- [ ] Report held-out semantic/schema/latency/resource/cancel metrics without an ungrounded 4B intelligence claim or production routing change.\n\n## Verification\n\nReview matrix/resource ceilings and deny-path tests first; admitted runs retain exact identity, fixtures, complete metrics and cleanup proofs; absent route/backend/admission stays blocked. These are future acceptance checks, not executed implementation evidence.\n\n## Risks\n\nRuntime identity drifts, tiny biased samples and resource contention can invalidate comparisons; endpoint observation is reported, not verified this session.\n\n## Source anchors\n\nDated planning evidence: 2026-11-03. Operator requirements are reported intent, not live runtime proof. Cross-repository absolute paths identify source ownership, not a promotion of domain authority.\n- /home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/qualify-the-bounded-colab-gemma-retrieval-research-pilot-and-retain-production-holdback.md\n- /home/err/docs/notes/design/epics-and-tasks.md\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- 0db50b53-6c7a-489a-bff9-048d57ce4cbb (S7A)\n- e616187d-ba13-42b1-addd-aa4d6244a5be (E6)\n\n## Initial runtime and NPU baseline update — 2026-11-03\n\nOperator-reported follow-up evidence (not remeasured by this planning writer): the expected local llama.cpp E4B endpoint on port8082 refuses connections, and the previously observed transient host runner on port45265 has disappeared. This supersedes any earlier description of that transient runner as currently active. Stable endpoint/runtime qualification is first, before any actual model quality claim; no E4B semantic baseline is established.\n\nThe NPU live baseline used 3 synthetic 960x600 images containing 9 lines: 9 valid boxes, but exact normalized text only 3/9, with reported inference 130–286 ms. Box/schema validity is not text accuracy or model semantic correctness. Semantic performance remains unmeasured. No private capture, cloud calls or 12B load occurred in the reported baseline. Future measurements require pinned runtime/model/mmproj/hash/hardware/time/context and resource admission; do not infer LLM NPU support from OCR.\n\nAdditional acceptance check: preserve this reported baseline with synthetic source/coordinate provenance, distinguish supplier timings from end-to-end latency, and deny model-quality conclusions until stable runtime qualification and independent held-out semantic evaluation exist. No new inference, capture, cloud request or model load is authorized by this card."}, :causal/root "7a08a09c-30c2-43e6-9376-2f872a44f867"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-3de19b00-adae-43e6-a6c4-da339faa6482-1793718672217", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:11:12.217Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "3de19b00-adae-43e6-a6c4-da339faa6482", :dependency ["3b9279b5-aafd-431a-90a9-128ce4415de0" "92b529b9-256d-4654-8aa6-5f1884a8adaa" "e616187d-ba13-42b1-addd-aa4d6244a5be" "e842e6d9-dd41-4ca2-b229-dc2466198864"], :parent nil, :card-type "epic", :type "task-created", :write-id "1793718672216-0.46te7656w8aij491bd2", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Oikos: consented labels and bounded Colab training corpus", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/oikos-consented-labels-and-bounded-colab-training-corpus-9faa6482.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Oikos: consented labels and bounded Colab training corpus\n\n## Context\n\nPlanning only for private open-hax/oikos at /home/err/spaces/foresight/oikos. Desktop is a local-first shared workbench. Initial incoming proposal; planning review is not complete. Creation authorizes no implementation, live configuration, deployment, inference, upload or spending.\n\n## Outcome\n\nProduce a consented reproducible corpus while retaining cloud spending, training and production holdbacks.\n\n## Scope\n\nAppend-only corrected labels, negative feedback, accepted/rejected actions and OCR boxes with consent/source hashes/privacy lineage. Dedupe by actual identity, not similarity. Train/dev/held-out splits grouped by temporal/app/source identity to prevent near-duplicate leakage. Reproducible JSONL/VLM coordinates, model/template/license. Export allowlist requires GovOne inspection and explicit approval before Google/Colab, which is cloud. Fresh budgets and teardown/resource proofs; link bounded pilot and its parent without inheriting its budget.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo new compute-unit spending, automatic training, automatic production adoption, private screenshot export or assumption old budget transfers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Corrections retain provenance and rejected-action/negative feedback history without silent similarity merges; consent and deletion lineage control payload availability.\n- [ ] Group split audit rejects near-duplicate leakage across source/app/time groups; exports pin coordinate, template, model and license versions.\n- [ ] GovOne inspection plus explicit approval and a fresh campaign/resource/teardown plan are mandatory before export or allocation; existing pilot and parent remain separate.\n\n## Verification\n\nSynthetic correction/dedupe/split/export tests; deny export without consent/policy/approval; dry-run budget/teardown proofs only and zero new allocation. These are future acceptance checks, not executed implementation evidence.\n\n## Risks\n\nCloud training exposes private data and can consume nonrefundable CU; historical pilot authority does not transfer to this corpus.\n\n## Source anchors\n\nDated planning evidence: 2026-11-03. Operator requirements are reported intent, not live runtime proof. Cross-repository absolute paths identify source ownership, not a promotion of domain authority.\n- /home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/qualify-the-bounded-colab-gemma-retrieval-research-pilot-and-retain-production-holdback.md\n- /home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/colab-browser-mcp-knoxx.md\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- 3b9279b5-aafd-431a-90a9-128ce4415de0 (E2)\n- 92b529b9-256d-4654-8aa6-5f1884a8adaa (E5)\n- e616187d-ba13-42b1-addd-aa4d6244a5be (E6)\n- e842e6d9-dd41-4ca2-b229-dc2466198864 (E7)\n- Related research (not inherited budget or completion authority): qualify-the-bounded-colab-gemma-retrieval-research-pilot-and-retain-production-holdback; parent da84a64d-f118-4722-8709-a1c556034f90."}, :causal/root "469d5507-dcf7-4a49-b086-fabe99e3c438"}
