{:event/type "kanban.frontmatter", :event/id "kanban-27ff00af-536d-4d7d-a9ad-a09b5ec2aaf3-1793718989289", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:16:29.289Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "27ff00af-536d-4d7d-a9ad-a09b5ec2aaf3", :key "dependency", :old-value ["29caa8e3-289a-416c-9850-8ef9cc769e88"], :new-value ["29caa8e3-289a-416c-9850-8ef9cc769e88" "c703893f-aea4-41c2-9eab-c3bd37b28c9b"], :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1793718989286-0.t3vcerbyysfjsrxvwgd", :type "frontmatter"}, :causal/root "3451f531-4302-43b6-badf-968fda6e1fbf"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-c703893f-aea4-41c2-9eab-c3bd37b28c9b-1793718989585", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:16:29.585Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "c703893f-aea4-41c2-9eab-c3bd37b28c9b", :text "Planning correction supersedes the original whole-E4 prerequisite and the original local_only verification wording “zero network calls.”\n\nDependencies: E2 (3b9279b5-aafd-431a-90a9-128ce4415de0) plus shared local capability S4A (29caa8e3-289a-416c-9850-8ef9cc769e88); the entire E4/client-matrix epic is not an execution prerequisite. GovOne admission must precede S4B qualification with real remote tool results. Only synthetic tests with no private data may precede that admission.\n\nCorrected acceptance criteria: local_only permits zero unauthorized cloud/third-party egress. Explicitly authenticated, allowlisted loopback/local-service transports may be used; a private IP address alone is not trusted and grants no authorization. Existing GovOne policy-session/scopes remain authoritative. Denied or unavailable routes fail closed, without direct-provider retry or fallback.\n\nCorrected verification: separately test an explicitly authenticated allowlisted local request that is permitted, an external destination denied in local_only, and unauthenticated/unallowlisted local or private-IP destinations denied. Cover expired scope, gateway outage and attempted fallback; no denied route is retried directly. This is an incoming planning correction, not completed verification or authorization for a live request.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1793718989582-0.g4sp4rgvg3vo7dps1z", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "5bbe41a6-1d23-46df-a8ac-c62da0432888"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-e616187d-ba13-42b1-addd-aa4d6244a5be-1793718989873", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:16:29.873Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "e616187d-ba13-42b1-addd-aa4d6244a5be", :text "Planning correction supersedes the original dependency on the whole E4 epic. The security foundation depends on E2 (3b9279b5-aafd-431a-90a9-128ce4415de0) and the shared local capability S4A (29caa8e3-289a-416c-9850-8ef9cc769e88), not completion of all client integrations. S6A admits the GovOne session gate before S4B real remote tool-result qualification. Synthetic no-private-data tests may precede admission; real local text/images/derived labels/tool payloads may not bypass it. Parent hierarchy is organization, not an implicit requirement to finish E4 before its local capability child can execute. No status advancement, implementation completion or live admission is claimed.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1793718989871-0.bzfdp9vkgdf68mx335h", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "e80f48ee-51df-4e23-9691-04ba01eecabd"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-27ff00af-536d-4d7d-a9ad-a09b5ec2aaf3-1793718990150", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:16:30.150Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "27ff00af-536d-4d7d-a9ad-a09b5ec2aaf3", :text "Planning correction supersedes the original S4A-only dependency and any acceptance reading that permits ungoverned real remote tool-result qualification. Dependencies are S4A (29caa8e3-289a-416c-9850-8ef9cc769e88) plus S6A (c703893f-aea4-41c2-9eab-c3bd37b28c9b). Real remote tool results and any local text/images/derived labels/tool payload crossing the cloud boundary require an admitted, authorized GovOne policy session before qualification. Only synthetic tests containing no private data may precede that admission; transport/auth and client integration success do not waive it. Verification must prove pre-admission denial and post-admission scoped handling separately for each client; blocked transport/auth remains a blocker. No real requests or completed qualification are claimed.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1793718990148-0.oxil0nbibkleyyesld", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "6a3cdcea-574a-4b27-a387-752fdccd06eb"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-456b2c69-cb5d-417d-9aeb-ac05e0a3251a-1793718990430", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:16:30.430Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "456b2c69-cb5d-417d-9aeb-ac05e0a3251a", :text "Planning correction supersedes any interpretation that the full E4 epic must finish before GovOne security admission, or that real remote client qualification can precede it. Keep E4 parent dependencies at E1 plus E2 only; do not add S6A to this parent. The remote admission gate is represented explicitly on S4B: S4A plus S6A. S6A and E6 depend on E2 plus S4A, not the entire E4. S4A is the shared local capability slice and does not require prior completion of its parent E4 or remote client matrix. This avoids a hierarchy-induced execution cycle while gating real remote tool results through an admitted GovOne session. Only synthetic no-private-data tests may precede remote admission. This comment is an incoming planning correction, not completed review or execution evidence.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1793718990428-0.nfckyhv0ticoutu8ef3", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "d8bb7310-3fe5-4433-9d34-d69f2a0762e4"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-0e124c65-694e-44f1-9959-ee83e81ca22b-1793718990714", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:16:30.714Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "0e124c65-694e-44f1-9959-ee83e81ca22b", :text "Planning correction supersedes qualitative-only resource acceptance and verification. Before any admitted execution, require a versioned, frozen resource profile specifying memory and CPU limits, maximum queued frames and total queued bytes, overflow behavior, inference deadline, and maximum pause/stop latency. Measure candidate thresholds in an isolated resource-admitted fixture, then freeze the selected profile and its identity before the admitted run; do not invent fixed numeric limits now or tune them silently during qualification.\n\nCorrected acceptance criteria: execution refuses a missing/unfrozen/incomplete profile; the profile covers every listed bound and the queue overflow policy. Corrected verification: overload and reconnect tests assert the configured memory/CPU/queue frame/byte bounds, declared overflow behavior, inference deadline and pause/stop latency; retain profile version/hash and measured results. Reconnect cannot discard resource admission or silently reset limits; violations are explicit failures. No resource measurement, inference or completed verification is claimed by this comment.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1793718990712-0.zb8p11vg5cdojbywbh", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "60a4e0f5-a00e-4d87-8901-13adf992a181"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-07452a65-4a6a-4704-bf81-50408927dcc8-1793718990979", :event/time "2026-11-03T15:16:30.979Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "07452a65-4a6a-4704-bf81-50408927dcc8", :text "Planning correction supplements and supersedes any single-runtime-only interpretation of shared-law verification. Acceptance requires the same shared CLJC law fixtures to pass in both Babashka (BB) and NBB, with fixture identity and each runtime's actual result retained. Explicit BB subprocess protocol tests must cover EDN framing, success and nonzero exits, malformed/truncated output, timeout and cancellation, including bounded termination/cleanup and truthful error propagation. No malformed output, timeout or cancelled child may be accepted as a successful rendered result. Cross-runtime law parity and subprocess protocol behavior are separate required checks; neither substitutes for the other. These are future acceptance/verification requirements, not tests run or completed implementation in this planning turn.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1793718990977-0.0ffffm0ykr7bwtplvfuh", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "ac010a06-d518-4a78-95e3-1cdc22e4778e"}
